https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/fci/1.0.2?topic=SSCKRH_1.0.2/platform/t_start_stop_kube_cluster.html

A. Stopping pods
1. % kubectl get pods

    NAME                                                    READY   STATUS                   RESTARTS        AGE

    imt-wr-consumer-service-deployment-686468b5fd-drmp5     1/1     Running                  0               7d3h
    imt-wr-producer-service-deployment-7c945d449f-shvp7     1/1     Running                  0               23d

2. scale the pod to 0
    % kubectl scale deploy imt-wr-consumer-service-deployment --replicas=0 -n telco
    % kubectl scale deploy imt-wr-producer-service-deployment --replicas=0 -n telco

3. Results
     % deployment.apps/imt-wr-consumer-service-deployment scaled
     % deployment.apps/imt-wr-producer-service-deployment scaled

B. Starting pods

1. Scale pod to 1
    % kubectl scale deploy imt-wr-consumer-service-deployment --replicas=1
    % kubectl scale deploy imt-wr-producer-service-deployment --replicas=1

3. Results
     % deployment.apps/imt-wr-consumer-service-deployment scaled
     % deployment.apps/imt-wr-producer-service-deployment scaled

4. % kubectl get pods

