II. API Management
From azure portal;
    1. Go to API Management services
    2. Select api-equity-dev
    3. Select Apis
    4. Add API
        - From the pop up window, add the Display name, and API URL Suffix eg broker-core
        - Create
    5. On Setting tab
        - Add Web service URL as broker main core loadBalancer External ip and the port - http://10.9.160.197:5001/ (This can be gotten from kubectl get services -o wide -n broker)
        - Deselect Subscription Required Option
    6. On Design tab
        i. Add operation for Frontend
            - Display Name - endpoint name like swagger
            - URL endpoint and Operation 
            - save
    7. On Test tab
        - for GET operation, no body is needed
        - for POST operation, add body
        - Send
        
III. Check pod logs

1. Run kubectl get pods -o wide -n broker 
2. Run kubectl logs -f <pod name> -n broker

